$DIR/main.p:3:1: expected declaration, found limit
    This line uses :=, the short variable declaration, outside a function. := is
    a statement, and statements may only appear inside a function body. Outside
    a function, a file may contain only declarations: package, import, const,
    var, type and func.
    To declare a package-level variable, use var:
        var limit = 10
    (see "Short variable declarations" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.11)
    (run "pluto explain E1003" for a longer explanation)
